The charge theorem states that the electric charge in units of e over three is a bijection from the pair consisting of the mode coordinate and the sign of the zero-state amplitude, to the five Standard Model charge eigenvalues: minus three, minus one, zero, plus two, and plus three. The three sigma-lines carry charges zero, plus five, and minus eight, which sum to minus one in units of the electron charge. The associated charge density on the torus is exactly four-by-four periodic. See HCSM-24 and HCSM-25.

