The mass map is an exponential function of the N-over-four label, with an amplitude of two hundred and twenty-four and a rate of zero point five four one one nine seven. The map reproduces the twelve charged fermion masses at root-mean-square zero point zero four four nine dex, which is approximately eleven percent accuracy, with zero free parameters. The N-over-four labels are derived from the mode coordinates by the delta function. See HCSM-23 and HCSM-33.

