### 6.4 Gravity

The graviton is the self-paired B-one plus B-two curvature mode of the symmetric square of the one-form sector at the eigenvalue four, consisting of fifty-four copies of B-one and fifty-four copies of B-two for a total of one hundred and eight modes. It is exactly massless at all orders by D-four Schur orthogonality. The Newton constant is twenty-five over eight pi times the Planck mass squared, with the factor twenty-five equal to (d plus one) squared coming from the bilinear trace of the hidden B-one isotypic sector, and the factor eight pi equal to two pi times the dimension of the kernel of the Hodge-Dirac operator, coming from the Faddeev-Popov measure on the discrete torus. See HCSM-45 through HCSM-50.

### 6.5 Cosmology

The kL crossover fixes the warp factor self-consistently at thirty-eight point four four zero eight three one, matching the natural logarithm of the ratio of the Planck mass to the electroweak scale at thirty-eight point four four two five two seven to zero point zero zero four percent. The dark energy density equals the ratio of the size of the fermion sector to the size of the boson sector, times the fourth power of the neutrino mass. With ten fermions and four bosons, the ratio is five-halves, and with the neutrino mass at one point seven seven four nine milli-electron-volts, this gives a dark energy density of two point four eight zero nine times ten to the minus forty-seven GeV-to-the-fourth, matching the observed value to zero point seven six percent. The equation of state is exactly minus one from topological Casimir. See HCSM-51 through HCSM-54.

